※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 8501 IMPL_BACKEND_UNSUPPORTED

※ Seeing that a product of two whole registers went past the end needs the
※ upper half of it, which two of the three architectures have as a single
※ instruction and the third has only in a form with a fixed pair of registers.
※ Refused on every target, so that a program means the same thing wherever it
※ is compiled.

let big: u64 = 4294967296u64

@[visible]
let answer: mut u64 = 0u64

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    answer ← big ⊠ big
    0u8
